    "note": "candidate-002 — FIX for the quantization the human caught in candidate-001 (some cells wider than others). Root cause: the full-canvas placeRects grid was passed as the SCALED content, so compose() ran it through insetNode (a scaled child cell) and the 4px-aligned split weights got re-quantized into the smaller inset rect → fractional-remainder spread across cells. Fix: pass the grid as a full-canvas extraLayer (compose(EMPTY, grid)) like the line-chart plot + donut ring — the grid now renders at EXACT canvas pixel coords, no rescale. Verified: all 56 cells are now exactly 68px wide (uniform). Everything else unchanged from c001.",
